# FIXED 2026-08-27 (the review's finding C, BUGS.md sec 16): this
# file now vets INVALID, as its `expected` line always said it
# should. Kept as the regression guard; the shared rows are
# vet-sizing-* in test/spec/vet.tsv.
#
# C5 (use-cases 05, 09): a sizing atom that shares a conjunct with a
# container (the ubiquitous template idiom) folds against that layer's
# container ALONE as soon as the schema settles; members from the vet
# data document (or an @ include, or a later pack) are never counted.
# A schema-satisfiable bound silently vanishes: --canon of this file
# alone already shows {"x":{&:{"r":integer}}} -- length(max(2)) gone.
# expected: verdict: invalid, exit 1 (three entries against max(2);
#           reference-language.md "Sizing atoms fold last": "after every
#           value that could contribute a member")
# actual: verdict: valid, exit 0. NOTE: a BARE atom in the schema
#         (x: length(max(2)) with no template beside it) IS re-checked
#         against data and correctly refuses -- the fold is early only
#         when a container sits in the same conjunct.
# run: aontu vet sizing-max-vanishes.aon three-entries.json
x: length(max(2)) & { &: {r: integer} }
